Title: Gaze waits for its seat roster through one shared bounded helper
Created: 2026-10-28
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-10-28T20:26Z claude created

--- body ---

## Context
Every gaze fork hand-writes its own collection loop over `.panel/<pr>/`
(`skills/gaze/references/fork-contract.md`, `panel.md` step 3): a fork lives
only while it calls tools, so the wait must be a tool call, and the recipe
leaves its shape to each session. Measured 2026-10-28 over 14 days of Claude
Code transcripts (3379 files): sleep-poll loops are the largest slow-call
class, and `.panel/` waits are most of them (211 of 280 on 2026-10-27, 75 of
106 on 2026-10-28; 1216's instruction route merged 2026-10-26 did not lower
the count). Variants seen: `for i in $(seq 1 55)`, `until [ -f a ] && [ -f b ]`,
`while [ $SECONDS -lt $end ]`, inline Python `time.sleep`, some running into
the 600 s tool cap and re-issued (one loop shape repeated 28 times within
single sessions). Durations are upper bounds (tool_use to tool_result).

Codex, same window (656 sessions): only 14 shell `.panel` waits; it polls
through its native `sleep` tool instead (2675 calls of 45-60 s, 40 sessions,
~34.8 h requested), 566 of them followed by `list_agents` although
`wait_agent` exists. Pi transcripts were not read.

The helper is a plain script, so it serves Claude Code, Codex and Pi alike;
it is not a guard (0976's burden of proof is not engaged).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One helper (e.g. `scripts/wait-roster.py <dir> --roster FILE|NAMES
      --deadline S`) blocks until every roster name exists as `<name>.md`
      (never `.part`), or the deadline passes; stays under the runtime's
      per-call cap and says so; exit 0 all present, 1 deadline with the
      missing names listed, 2 usage
- [ ] `fork-contract.md` and `panel.md` step 3 (and any other skill that
      collects seat files, e.g. verify-adherence) call it instead of
      describing a hand-written loop; the 15-minute gaze deadline is honoured
      across re-issued calls
- [ ] Tests: all-present, deadline with a missing name, `.part` ignored
- [ ] `make check` passes
